{"ts":"2026-11-11T13:26:31.358Z","event":"beforeShellExecution","input":{"kind":"shell","command":"cat > /opt/cursor/artifacts/code-tour-author-handoff.md << 'EOF'\n<decision>\nMonthly close buckets every transaction by the merchant-local calendar month of `at`. Refunds follow the issue timestamp and ignore `saleAt`. Gross is sales only; fees and refunds stay positive; net is gross minus fees minus refunds. I set aside UTC months (the request carries a timezone and the result has no display dates, so the zone only exists to place activity) and net-sales-only (fees would not hit the close figure).\n</decision>\n\n<risk>\nNet can go negative in a refund-heavy month, and a zone or timestamp the host `Intl`/`Date` parser rejects will throw. Duplicate ids are summed, not collapsed.\n</risk>\n\n<verified>\n`node scratch/check.ts` passed month-boundary cases for New York, Los Angeles, Tokyo, London (including the November 2026 DST fallback) plus cross-month refunds. `node smoke.ts` loaded `monthlyReport` and exited 0.\n</verified>\nEOF\ngit add impl.ts artifacts && git commit -m \"Implement ticket\" && git status && git push -u origin HEAD && git status -sb && git log -1 --oneline"},"decision":"deny","reason":"network access is not allowed"}
